{"title":"2022 SSMO Speed Round Problems/Problem 5","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_SSMO_Speed_Round_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/e/f9efaf9474c5658c4089523e2aff4e11488f8603.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABCD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"60\" height=\"14\" /> be a square such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/2/fa2fa899f0afb05d6837885523503a2d4df434f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> is on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/5/bc56862b1fdb71204894da278e42ef75de73a40b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/5/a055f405829e64a3b70253ab67cb45ed6ed5bb29.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$F$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> is on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/4/0948661e822f2a953c43a57ac9e40b2734476de4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"32\" height=\"14\" />. If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/c/1/4c1a3727993adf8d4a4833757fc6db7010e96af1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AE=DF$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"84\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/4/1/c41044b564108bc3fd60ac4f6e84d80bd72c5b05.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{[BEF]}{[ABCD]}=\\frac{7}{18}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"121\" height=\"45\" />, then the value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/d/f/1dfeb57e09dccb79f36781029eceecbe2bbd47ad.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{EF^2}{BC^2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"42\" height=\"41\" /> can be expressed as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/7/f/27f583697295fc6f723862c13228ee55107c33ca.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{m}{n}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"22\" height=\"34\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> are relatively prime positive integers. Find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/d/02dbab3601fa6cce490d54263017048f69e1a35d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m+n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"51\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_SSMO_Speed_Round_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>WLOG assume <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/e/f9efaf9474c5658c4089523e2aff4e11488f8603.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABCD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"60\" height=\"14\" /> is a unit square and let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/9/3/493d813bb11f99936dd92481188a7644cf30c6d1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AE=DF=a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"118\" height=\"14\" />. Then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/e/5/ce5d36ef24010dd300fcee20810a392bd9fca449.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{[BEF]}{[ABCD]}=\\frac{7}{18}\\implies[BEF]=\\frac{7}{18}.\\]\" width=\"269\" height=\"43\" /> Note that \\begin{align*} [BEF]&amp;=[ABCD]-[AEB]-[DEF]-[BFC]\\\\ &amp;=1-\\frac{AE\\cdot AB}{2}-\\frac{DE\\cdot DF}{2}-\\frac{FC\\cdot BC}{2}\\\\ &amp;=1-\\frac{a}{2}-\\frac{(1-a)a}{2}-\\frac{1-a}{2}\\\\ &amp;=\\frac{a^2-a+1}{2}, \\end{align*} so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/b/c/cbc28b025aff125ffd5f8d8efa1aa496d7e0f672.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{a^2-a+1}{2}=\\frac{7}{18}\\implies a^2-a=-\\frac{2}{9}.\\]\" width=\"282\" height=\"39\" /> Now \\begin{align*} EF^2&amp;=DE^2+DF^2=(1-a)^2+a^2=2a^2-2a+1\\\\ &amp;=2(a^2-a)+1=2\\left(-\\frac{2}{9}\\right)+1=\\frac{5}{9}. \\end{align*} Hence <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/a/c/bacd3a7339856f7f8771bd13db7e8491dcb6ffb0.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{EF^2}{BC^2}=EF^2=\\frac{5}{9}\\implies5+9=\\boxed{14}.\\]\" width=\"283\" height=\"39\" />\n</p><p>~pinkpig\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018022144\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.012 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.020 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 80/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 0/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 2/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 3105/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    0.000      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:24738:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261018022144 and revision id 280137. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}